# profile.kb . Repository Knowledge Base

> Single-page map of this repository: what every file and folder does, what kind of
> information it stores, how content flows from edit to published GitHub profile, and
> where the canonical numbers live.
>
> Generated by inspection of the working tree at `VERSION` **0.1.0**, branch `main`.
> Regenerate this page whenever the directory layout, the deploy deny-list, or the
> check scripts change.

---

## 1. What this repository is

This is the **source of truth for a public personal-brand profile** . the markdown
content set for **Ali Abdullah Khan** (GitHub `hellsalve017196`), **VP of Software
Engineering at JP Morgan Chase**, based in Holbrook, New York.

It is a **content repository, not an application.** Its job is to hold ~65 markdown
pages, validate them with three plain-Node linters, and mirror the allow-listed subset
into the special `<owner>/<owner>` GitHub profile repo (`hellsalve017196/hellsalve017196`)
so that `README.md` renders as the GitHub profile page.

Three consumers read this content:

| Consumer | What it reads | How |
|---|---|---|
| **GitHub profile page** | `README.md` plus every relatively-linked `.md` | mirrored by `.github/workflows/deploy-profile.yml` |
| **Humans evaluating Ali** | `ali-abdullah-khan-profile.md`, `experience/`, `systems/`, `skills/` | read directly in the repository |
| **Search and answer engines** | `why-hire/`, `faq/`, `skills/`, `writing/` | answer pages, each opening with a `TL;DR` |

The editorial stance is declared up front. [`disclaimer.md`](./disclaimer.md) states
that the copy is compiled from Ali's public site and public GitHub history, edited with
automation help, and written for discoverability . and, critically, that **JP Morgan
Chase is not the author, editor, or publisher of anything here**. That notice is not
left to reviewer discipline: `scripts/check-structure.js` fails the build if a page
names the firm and omits it.

