## 4. File reference

### 4.1 Canonical entry points

| File | What it does | Information stored |
|---|---|---|
| `README.md` | The GitHub profile page. 15 numbered sections (`1. Ali Now` → `15. Why Hire … Answer Pages`), preceded by a "Who is Ali Abdullah Khan?" block. | Headline + role, two shields.io badge walls (status and core skills), bio block, current focus, the `working-with-ali` short list, condensed experience timeline, writing index, open-source/hardware list, discussion topics, skills summary, `<!-- PROFILES -->` block, systems list, engineering practices, learning, hire/FAQ/answer-page hubs, managed disclaimer footer. |
| `ali-abdullah-khan-profile.md` | Long-form **mirror** of the README. 15 sections, hand-maintained `<!-- toc -->`. | The same claim set with more room: a longer bio, per-role detail with stacks, the writing table, the five-era GitHub journey, a four-row skills table, education/certification, the systems table, `<!-- PROFILES -->` block, and a *Trust & Verification* section pointing at the meta layer. |
| `profile.kb` | This knowledge base. | Repository structure, file purposes, conventions, canonical-data index, pipeline description, verified observations. |
| `tone.md` | Writing-pattern analysis. | The evidence base and its limits, 8 signature habits, sentence-length distribution over 590 sentences, page architecture shares, punctuation rules (em dashes banned; `X . Y` substitute), self-reference rules, a "writing in Ali's pattern" checklist, and a stratum identification key. |

### 4.2 Trust & meta layer

| File | What it does | Information stored |
|---|---|---|
| `disclaimer.md` | The accuracy and liability notice. Target of the `<!-- DISCLAIMER -->` block on 60 pages. | What the repository is; **the employer notice** (JP Morgan Chase is not author/editor/publisher, nothing here is a firm statement, no internal architecture is disclosed); a list of the specific claims to treat as summaries (`~1M daily users`, "full WCAG compliance", the 30/70 split, "Associate to VP in under four years", years-of-experience figures, self-assessed tiers, repository snapshot date); the editorial method; and contact routes for verification. |
| `proof-sources.md` | Single canonical citation index. | **10 primary sources**: alikhan.dev, GitHub (72 repos, Pull Shark, Arctic Code Vault), LinkedIn (both URLs), the AWS Cloud Practitioner cert (Sep 2023), North South University, the six blog posts, and four specific repositories (`official_website`, the adhan clock, `ai-job-search`, `LirrTrainTracker`). Plus the two in-repo source KBs, an explicit **"what is *not* independently sourced"** section, and a three-step "how to challenge a claim" procedure. |
| `profile-setup.md` | Ops runbook for the publish pipeline. **Not linked from README**, excluded from deploy. | What ships vs. what does not; the workflow table; one-time setup (create `<owner>/<owner>`, mint a fine-grained PAT, add `PROFILE_DEPLOY_TOKEN`, optional `PROFILE_REPO` / `PROFILE_BRANCH`); local commands; the release ritual; the managed-block table; and 4 known gaps. |
| `CHANGELOG.md` | Machine-level release detail, newest first. | Added/Changed sections plus a `### Verified` block quoting the **real** linter output for the release. |
| `release-notes.md` | Narrative version of the same release. | Prose summary, where the content came from, the reasoning behind the trust layer, three deliberate departures from the reference pattern, and pending follow-ups. |
| `VERSION` | Single-line semver (`0.1.0`). | Nothing else. Bumped alongside a CHANGELOG entry. |

### 4.3 Source knowledge bases

These two files are **research notes kept in-repo**, so any claim on the profile can be
traced without re-researching it. They are the only files that use em dashes, and they
are written in a neutral analytical register rather than the profile voice.

| File | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `profile.md` | Analysis of [alikhan.dev](https://alikhan.dev) as of **2026-10-04**: identity table, headline highlights, published bio, three roles with bullets, the skills table, education and certification, all six blog posts with summaries and tags, and the site's technical details (Astro 5.18.2, nginx VPS → Cloudflare Pages, 8 URLs, JSON-LD, RSS). |
| `github.md` | Analysis of [github.com/hellsalve017196](https://github.com/hellsalve017196) as of **2026-10-04**: profile table, tech-stack rollup by layer, 12 flagship projects with detail, the **full 72-repository inventory grouped by era**, a five-era journey analysis, and the contribution-activity breakdown. |

