| `singledoor-payment-rails.mmd` | Mermaid `flowchart TB`: consumer → unified front door (UI, accessibility gate, feature flags) → three payment rails → operate (idempotency, SLOs, rollback). **Conceptual only** . no internal architecture is represented |

### 4.13 Tooling . `scripts/`

| Script | What it checks | npm script |
|---|---|---|
| `check-links.js` | Walks every `.md`; verifies relative file links resolve on disk, `#anchor` fragments exist (as headings or `<a id>`), and `<img src>` / `![]()` targets exist. Skips `http(s)`, `mailto:`, `tel:`, `data:`. Rejects absolute internal paths. | `check:links` |
| `check-filenames.js` | In the 8 content dirs: filenames must match `^[a-z0-9._-]+\.md$`, must not carry a `-vNN` suffix, and **`experience/` pages must carry a zero-padded `NN-` prefix**. Root GitHub-standard names are exempt. | `check:filenames` |
| `check-structure.js` | Per content page: the managed `DISCLAIMER` block is present, in order, and links to `disclaimer.md`; **any page naming JP Morgan Chase states the "not the author, editor, or publisher" notice inside that block**; back-navigation exists (entry points exempt); exactly one `H1`. | `check:structure` |
| `deploy-profile.sh` | **Deny-list only**, from `.deployignore`. Copies everything except `.git/` and the matched patterns. Runs `npm run check:links` first unless `SKIP_LINK_CHECK=1`. This is the script CI uses. | `deploy:profile` |
| — | Aggregate gate: `check:filenames && check:structure && check:links` | **`check:profile`** |

**`check-structure.js` is the one that justifies the suite.** The other two enforce
tidiness; this one enforces the employer notice, which is a legal-adjacent requirement
rather than a style preference.

### 4.14 Build, CI, deploy

| File | What it does |
|---|---|
| `.github/workflows/ci.yml` | 2 jobs on PR + push to `main`: **check-profile** (`npm run check:profile` on Node 20) and **lychee-link-check** (external URLs, accepting 200/201/202/204/206/403/429/999). No install step . the scripts have no dependencies. |
| `.github/workflows/deploy-profile.yml` | On push to `main` touching `**/*.md`, `diagrams/**`, `.deployignore`, the deploy script, or itself (plus `workflow_dispatch`): checks out this repo and the target profile repo (`vars.PROFILE_REPO`, default `<owner>/<owner>`; `vars.PROFILE_BRANCH`, default `main`) using `secrets.PROFILE_DEPLOY_TOKEN`, runs the deploy script with `SKIP_LINK_CHECK=1`, then commits `profile: sync from <repo>@<sha>` if the tree changed. Serialised by `concurrency: deploy-profile`. |
| `.deployignore` | Deny-list: `CV.md`, all `*.pdf`, `node_modules/`, `.github/`, `scripts/`, `package.json`, the dotfiles, `prompt.md`, `.playwright-mcp/`, `.claude/`, and the five repo-internal meta docs (`profile.kb`, `tone.md`, `profile-setup.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`, `release-notes.md`, `VERSION`). One glob per line, case-insensitive, matched against repo-relative paths. |
| `.lycheeignore` | URL regexes lychee must skip: all of `linkedin.com` (returns HTTP 999 to bots) and `docs.google.com` (frequently gated). |
| `.markdownlint.json` | MD013/MD033/MD034/MD036/MD041/MD045 disabled; MD024 siblings-only; MD049/MD050 asterisk. **Advisory . nothing invokes markdownlint** (see §8). |
| `.gitignore` | OS/editor/Node noise, plus local scratch (`.playwright-mcp/`, `.claude/`, `prompt.md`) and the private-document rules (`CV.md`, `*.pdf`) that also appear in the deny-list. |
| `package.json` | Name `ali-abdullah-khan-profile`, private, `type: module`, Node ≥ 20. **Zero dependencies** . the authoritative list of `check:*` scripts and nothing else. |

