## 5. Content conventions

Rules a new or edited page is expected to follow (✅ = enforced by `scripts/`):

1. **Managed blocks . never hand-edit between the markers:**
   - `<!-- DISCLAIMER:START -->` … `END` . on 60 pages. Presence, ordering, the link to `disclaimer.md`, and the employer notice are all ✅.
   - `<!-- PROFILES:START -->` … `END` . the canonical link list in `README.md` and the mirror profile. **Edit both together.**
   - `<!-- toc -->` … `<!-- /toc -->` . hand-maintained, in the mirror profile, `faq.md`, and `working-with-ali.md`.
   - `<!-- last-reviewed -->` . on 7 pages; bumped during the release ritual.
2. **Filenames** ✅ . lowercase `[a-z0-9._-]`, no `-vNN` suffix. `experience/` uses a zero-padded `NN-` timeline prefix.
3. **Page shape** ✅ . exactly one `H1`; back-navigation present (`README.md` and the mirror profile exempt); disclaimer block last.
4. **New SEO/answer pages open with `## TL;DR`**; system and project pages open with a `> **TL;DR**` blockquote.
5. **Em dashes are banned in profile prose.** The substitute is a spaced period (`X . Y`). The only files containing em dashes are the two source KBs, `profile.md` and `github.md`. See [`tone.md`](./tone.md) §6.
6. **Links** ✅ . relative paths and `#anchors` must resolve. Absolute internal paths are rejected.
7. **Badges** . shields.io URLs, deep-linked to the `<a id>` anchors at the bottom of the text-format skill matrix. **No local image files** . that is deliberate, so there is no binary asset set to drift.
8. **Tooltips are written, not generated.** Every `title=` and markdown hover title is hand-written for its link. There is no template pool and no rotation script.
9. **Naming** . "Ali Abdullah Khan" in full on first mention per page and in headings, "Ali" thereafter. Normal pronoun use. First person only inside `writing/`.
10. **Employer discipline.** Any page naming JP Morgan Chase carries the notice ✅, and no page may describe internal architecture, internal metrics, or non-public information beyond what is already published on alikhan.dev.
11. **Release ritual** . bump `VERSION`, add a `CHANGELOG.md` entry with a `### Verified` block quoting real linter output, add a `release-notes.md` narrative, bump the `last-reviewed` dates, refresh this file if the layout changed.

