## 7. How content flows

```
edit markdown
   │
   ▼
npm run check:profile ──► check:filenames → check:structure → check:links
   │
   ▼
push to main
   │
   ├─ ci.yml ................... check-profile · lychee-link-check
   └─ deploy-profile.yml ....... deploy-profile.sh → hellsalve017196/hellsalve017196
                                    │                  → git commit + push
                                    ▼
                          github.com/hellsalve017196
                          (README.md renders as the profile page)
```

Local dry run:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/hellsalve017196/hellsalve017196 ../hellsalve017196
npm run deploy:profile -- ../hellsalve017196
```

---

## 8. Verified observations

Each item was confirmed by running the tooling or grepping the tree . recorded as
findings, not as changes.

| # | Observation | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | All three checks pass cleanly. | `[check-filenames] OK (experience, skills, projects, systems, writing, faq, why-hire, learning)`; `[check-structure] OK (59 content pages: disclaimer block, employer notice, back-nav, single H1)`; `[check-links] OK` |
| 2 | **Zero em dashes in the 61 profile-content pages.** The only hits repository-wide are in the source KBs: `profile.md` (17) and `github.md` (33), which are research notes, not profile prose. | `grep -c '—'` per file |
| 3 | **Zero binary assets.** All 73 badge references are shields.io URLs, so there is no icon directory to duplicate or drift . the single most common failure mode in profile repositories of this shape. | `find . -type f -not -name '*.md' -not -name '*.mmd'` returns only config and scripts |
| 4 | **`package.json` has no dependencies**, and the three linters import nothing outside `node:fs` / `node:path`. `ci.yml` therefore runs no install step and no lockfile is needed. | `package.json`; the `import` lines in `scripts/*.js` |
| 5 | `deploy-profile.yml` **will fail until the one-time setup is done** . the target repo `hellsalve017196/hellsalve017196` and the `PROFILE_DEPLOY_TOKEN` secret do not exist yet. `ci.yml` is unaffected. | `profile-setup.md` §4; `release-notes.md` pending follow-ups |
| 6 | The deploy script is **deny-list only**, so anything new at the repository root ships unless `.deployignore` is updated in the same commit. The PowerShell/allow-list variant present in the reference pattern was deliberately not carried over . one deploy path, one behaviour. | `scripts/deploy-profile.sh`; `.deployignore` |
| 7 | `.markdownlint.json` exists but **nothing invokes markdownlint** . no workflow, script, or `package.json` entry. It is there for editor integration. | `grep -rn markdownlint .` finds no hits outside the config |
| 8 | **Two LinkedIn URLs are in circulation** (`in/abdullah017196` from the website, `in/ali-abdullah-khan-636a919a` from the GitHub profile). Both are listed in the `<!-- PROFILES -->` block because the canonical one is unconfirmed. | `profile.md` vs `github.md`; tracked in `release-notes.md` |
| 9 | `lychee` **cannot verify the LinkedIn or Google Docs links** . both patterns are skipped in `.lycheeignore` because LinkedIn returns HTTP 999 to bots. Those URLs are therefore never actually checked by CI. | `.lycheeignore` |
| 10 | **Years-of-experience figures are derived, not asserted by the subject.** They come from public repository dates and role dates, and the skill matrix names its evidence per row so a reader can judge the gap between "first commit in a language" and "professional proficiency". This is stated in `disclaimer.md`. | `ali-abdullah-khan-tech-stack-skills-text-format.md`; `disclaimer.md` |
| 11 | **The 30/70 accessibility split is a single-program observation**, and all four pages that cite it say so in their disclaimer. It is the most citable-looking number on the profile and the easiest to mis-cite. | `systems/accessibility-definition-of-done.md`, `skills/accessibility.md`, `writing/accessibility-first-engineering-wcag-compliance.md`, `faq/is-accessibility-worth-the-engineering-cost.md` |
| 12 | `CHANGELOG.md`, `release-notes.md`, `profile-setup.md`, `profile.kb` and `tone.md` have **no inbound links from any profile page** . intentional. They are repo-internal meta docs and are excluded from the deploy. (`tone.md` and `profile.kb` are linked from the mirror profile's *Trust & Verification* section, which is the one deliberate exception.) | inbound-link sweep; `.deployignore` |
| 13 | **`check-structure.js` exempts the trust and meta pages** from the disclaimer rule, because `disclaimer.md` *is* the notice and the meta docs are not profile content. The exemption list is explicit in the script rather than pattern-based. | `EXEMPT` set in `scripts/check-structure.js` |

---

## 9. Task recipes

| Goal | Touch |
|---|---|
| Change the GitHub profile page | `README.md`, then `npm run check:profile` |
| Keep the long-form profile in sync | mirror the same edit into `ali-abdullah-khan-profile.md` |
| Add a role | new `experience/NN-….md` on the §4.4 shape; link it from README §3 and the mirror §4 |
| Add a system Ali built | new `systems/<slug>.md` on the §4.5 shape; add a row to README §9 and the mirror §9 table |
| Add a technology authority page | new `skills/<tech>.md` from the §4.6 template; add a badge in both tech-stack pages; **add the `<a id>` anchor** to the text-format matrix |
| Add a public project | new `projects/<slug>.md`; link it from README §5 and the mirror §6 table |
| Add a blog post | new `writing/<slug>.md`; add a row to `writing.md`, README §4, and the mirror §5 table |
| Add an FAQ answer | short → a numbered entry in `faq.md` **and its `<!-- toc -->`**; long → `faq/<slug>.md` plus links from `faq.md` and README §13 |
| Add an answer/geo page | `why-hire/<slug>.md` opening with `## TL;DR`; link from README §15 and the mirror §14 |
| Change a proficiency tier | `ali-abdullah-khan-tech-stack-skills-text-format.md` **and** the matching `skills/*.md` italic line |
| Add a diagram | `diagrams/<name>.mmd`; reference it from the page it illustrates |
| Add a proof or citation | `proof-sources.md`; link there from the page instead of inlining a proof block |
| Change the disclaimer wording | `disclaimer.md` for the full notice; the per-page blocks are short pointers and must keep the employer-notice phrase or `check:structure` fails |
| Cut a release | bump `VERSION` → `CHANGELOG.md` entry with a `### Verified` block → `release-notes.md` narrative → bump `last-reviewed` on 7 pages → refresh this file |
| Publish manually | *Actions → Deploy GitHub profile → Run workflow*, or `npm run deploy:profile -- ../hellsalve017196` |

